.TH DIPICAM378 1 "2026-08-17" "dvbipitools" "dvbipitools Manual"
.SH NAME
dipicam378 \- cs378x (camd35/TCP) key server for CAS testing
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dipicam378
.B \-k
.I keyfile
[\fIoptions\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B dipicam378
is a cs378x (camd35/TCP) key server: it holds a device's RSA private key
and answers ECM/EMM requests with a control word. It is a software
smartcard, nothing more.
.PP
The tool speaks the cs378x/camd35 protocol used by oscam-compatible
card readers. It listens on a TCP port, accepts a connection from a
cs378x client such as oscam, and services ECM/EMM requests using a
locally-held PEM-encoded RSA private key for a single device. The
protocol's AES-128 encryption key is derived from the digest of the
configured password, which must match the reader's \fBpassword =\fR
setting.
.PP
.B dipicam378
is intended for testing and validation of
.BR dipitvhead (1)'s
and
.BR dipiradiohead (1)'s
CAS output: it pairs with those tools' encrypted multicast streams and
lets an oscam-driven client descramble them as if a real smartcard were
present. It is not built without libssl, since RSA/AES crypto is its
sole purpose.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-k ", " \-\-key\ \fI<path>\fR
RSA private key, PEM. Required.
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-serial\ \fI<id>\fR
Device's serial, matched against EMM-U.
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-port\ \fI<n>\fR
cs378x TCP listen port. Default: \fB27500\fR.
.TP
.BR \-a ", " \-\-auth\ \fI[user:]<pass>\fR
Password must match the reader's \fBpassword =\fR (default:
\fBdipicam378\fR); its digest is the AES-128 key.
.TP
.B \-\-caid \fI<hex>\fR
ECMs for any other CAID get a CMD08 ("stop asking"). Optional, default:
no CMD08 ever sent.
.TP
.B \-\-algo \fI<a>\fR
.IR cissa | csa2 .
Default: \fBcissa\fR.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Protocol/decode detail on stderr.
.TP
.B \-\-color \fI<when>\fR
.IR auto | always | never .
Default: \fBauto\fR.
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-daemonize
Fork to background after startup, detach from terminal.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show usage and exit.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B dipicam378 \-k device.key \-s e2e-01 \-p 27500
Serve a single device's key on the default cs378x port, filtering EMM-U
by serial.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B 0
on success.
A non-zero status is returned on argument errors or socket failure.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR dipitvhead (1),
.BR dipiradiohead (1),
.BR dipidescramble (1)
.PP
